        "searchText": "A local-search plan, without the bankruptcy story Sarvesh describes a local-SEO plan he would use if he had to rebuild income: pages and profiles that match how nearby buyers search. The $100k-a-month line is his claim. Local search is ordinary search pointed at a place. The page has to name the service and the place a buyer would type. Write one service-plus-place phrase a nearby buyer might type. Sketch three local pages you would need (for example a main service page, a specific job page, and a place page) and the unique title for each. Do not create business profiles or spend on ads. You can explain how local pages differ from a generic homepage, and you have treated Sarvesh’s income claim as a claim. A concrete example What to do You're done when A rebuild-from-zero local plan focuses on pages and profiles that match how nearby buyers search for a service in a place. Sarvesh frames the plan as a way he would get to $100,000 a month if he woke up bankrupt. That income target is his claim."
