        "searchText": "Research bots for short video, not autoposters jaffa describes ten bots that watch a large video database and turn what they find into a weekly plan. The useful idea is research and a human who still chooses what to film. A bot that finds outlier openings and competitor ads is a research assistant. A bot that posts without you is a different, riskier product. Write one question you would want a research bot to answer each Monday, such as “which openings in this niche got saved last week?” List five research jobs from jaffa’s set (scan outliers, propose ideas, watch competitors, turn voice notes into scripts, plan the week) and mark which ones you would allow to run unattended versus which must stay drafts. You can separate research automation from autoposting, and you know this module is optional and tool-specific. What to do You're done when jaffa’s ten-bot setup scans a large viral-video database for outlier openings and formats, proposes ideas, tracks competitor posts and ads, turns voice notes into scripts, and has one bot assemble a weekly plan."
