        "excerpt": "Korzhov lists eleven operator skills from ads agents to incrementality. Cody argues the “100x marketer” now outranks the “100x engineer” if they can wire tools. Both posts also sell software. Take the map, leave the pitch.",
        "searchText": "Marketing engineering as a stack, not a personality Korzhov lists eleven operator skills from ads agents to incrementality. Cody argues the “100x marketer” now outranks the “100x engineer” if they can wire tools. Both posts also sell software. Take the map, leave the pitch. You do not need eleven systems. You need to know the map so you do not confuse a missing tracking event with a missing strategy. Circle the one layer from Korzhov’s eleven that would unblock you first, or write “none yet.” Write Korzhov’s eleven steps as one line each in your own words. Mark each “core already covered,” “optional later,” or “does not apply.” Do not install his repo or Cody’s tools. You can see the stack and know which parts this course already taught. The eleven, in one line each What to do You're done when Korzhov’s eleven steps cover an ads agent with caps, programmatic SEO, AI video ads, rebuilding competitor winners, getting cited by assistants, large-scale review research, matching ads to landing pages, trustworthy conversion tracking, behavior-triggered messages with holdouts, incrementality, and a weekly report. Cody writes that the 100x marketer is now higher leverage than the 100x engineer, and promotes Graphed as a way to deploy marketing agents. Those are positioning claims and product promotions."
