        "excerpt": "DeepSeek’s writeup is about an always-on system that routes work to specialists instead of trapping every task in a separate chat. It is architecture, not a marketing channel.",
        "searchText": "Super-agent design, in plain words DeepSeek’s writeup is about an always-on system that routes work to specialists instead of trapping every task in a separate chat. It is architecture, not a marketing channel. Isolated chats do not scale past a handful of jobs. A router plus specialists is closer to how a small team already works. Write two jobs you would never put in the same chat, and why. Sketch a router and three named specialist roles on paper, including what each is forbidden to do. Do not build it. You can explain why session isolation becomes a management problem, and you know this module is optional architecture. What to do You're done when Mainstream agents still treat a single isolated session as the unit of work, and a person can usually follow only a few active sessions. A super-agent design routes incoming work to specialist workers and keeps the human at higher-level decisions."
