        "searchText": "A technical FOMO list, translated Suraj’s “cancel your weekend” list is a pile of agent-infrastructure techniques. It is not a marketing plan. This appendix names what the items are so they are not mistaken for launch tactics. Most items on that list are engineering reliability problems. Marketing still starts with a customer and a sentence they understand. Pick one item from the list and write whether it is marketing, product reliability, or neither. Group five listed techniques into “would help a marketer later,” “is only for builders,” or “I do not need this.” Stop after five. You can see the list as infrastructure, not as a weekend marketing assignment. A concrete translation What to do You're done when Suraj’s 2027 list includes computer-use agents, generative UI, a cheap/fast router for easy requests, durable workflows that can resume, an MCP server so other agents can call your product, constrained outputs, graders, injection proxies, privacy unmasking, cost kill-switches, and related serving tricks."
