        "searchText": "Your first month if you join a growth role Honorato’s first-month roadmap is for someone joining a company that already has product-market fit. The saved archive is partial. What remains is research first, then foundations rather than a bag of tactics. A new growth hire’s first job is understanding the company, not installing a stack of tricks. Write whether you are joining someone else’s company or building your own. The rest of the module only applies to the first case. Using only the saved research areas team, company analysis, and first quick win write three questions you would ask in week one. Do not invent later sections the archive cut off. You know this module is role-specific and partial, and you have not filled gaps the source does not contain. What “first win” means here What to do You're done when Before or during the first days, study team, company, and a possible first win so you understand structure, model, current strategy, competitors’ channels, and where a quick learning might sit. Foundations are built on principles, not tactics. The first month should reinforce process and learning, quoting Balfour’s line that Honorato repeats."
