        "searchText": "Seventy-seven brands, used as inspiration Robbie Richards collected early growth stories from many well-known companies. There is no single model. Use the catalog as inspiration, not as seventy-seven assignments to copy. Famous companies did not share one trick. They found a first channel that matched their situation, which is the same advice as the one-channel lesson. Write one famous-company story you already know, and one reason it might not fit your situation. Skim only the idea that there is no plug-and-play formula. Then write two first-customer ideas that would fit your constraints, without copying a named company’s play. You can treat the catalog as inspiration, not as a to-do list of 77 case studies. A concrete way to use a famous story What to do You're done when There is no one-size-fits-all model for getting first customers. Robbie’s catalog of 77 companies is offered as inspiration for demand generation, not as a single formula."
