        "excerpt": "Ryan (ryangrowthh)",
        "searchText": "Distribution 101: A Guide to Reaching Millions Ryan ryangrowthh x-article Start with the enemy, not with yourself Distribution is a series of chapters in a larger story. Good chapters make people feel something, teach something, and make them want the next one. Pick a vehicle for the story Building a brand is telling a series of chapters that fit a larger story, and each piece of organic content is one step on that path. Pick a vehicle for the story Vehicles are rented platforms you do not control, owned audiences you can reach directly, or earned attention from someone else’s audience. You eventually want all three, but you should not start everywhere. Pick a vehicle for the story Pick a first vehicle by asking where the audience already spends time, whether you write or talk more easily, and how much time you can really commit. Founder presence without becoming an influencer Founder-led content works when the person is living the next chapter of the story, not when they post announcements."
