        "searchText": "The 𝕏 Algorithm Explained, In Depth Ryan ryangrowthh x-article How X decides who sees a post X pulls candidate posts from Thunder (accounts you follow), Phoenix (posts that match your interests even if you do not follow the author), and SimClusters (posts popular with people like you). How X decides who sees a post A ranking model then predicts what a viewer will do and scores the post. In Ryan’s 30 October 2026 table, copy-link shares weight 20, replies and quotes 5, follows 4, likes 0.66, and profile clicks 0. Reports and mutes are large negatives. How X decides who sees a post Ryan reports very large lifetime impressions and fast recent growth on his own account. Those are his results."
