        "excerpt": "borja (borjafat)",
        "searchText": "Rank #1 With Claude SO Fast People Think You Hacked Google borja borjafat x-article Improve what already almost ranks Title tests belong on pages already near the top that get impressions but few clicks. Write at least three titles with the searcher’s words first, a specific promise, a reason to click, under about 60 characters, and nothing the page does not deliver. Improve what already almost ranks On Borja’s site, titles that used the words people typed got a 4.7 percent click-through rate, while titles that only named the category got under 1 percent. Improve what already almost ranks Judge a title test by clicks as well as click-through rate, compare similar positions, and change one thing at a time. Optional paid title tests with ads are a speed tactic, not a required exercise. Trust what you measure Change one thing at a time, write the starting numbers down, and compare similar conditions so a rank change cannot masquerade as a title win."
