        "searchText": "The cold email cheat sheet: Christian coldemailchris x-post How to read a cold-email report without sending one Christian’s cheat sheet maps outcomes to causes no replies and no bounces suggests the mail never landed, replies without interest suggest the offer, bounces over about 2 percent suggest the list, and open rate is a tracking pixel that can hurt inbox placement. How to read a cold-email report without sending one He reports rough benchmarks such as one lead per 300 contacts as a great campaign, one per 500 as still solid, Google-hosted prospects replying much more than Microsoft-hosted ones, very short copy for Microsoft prospects, and near-zero replies for generic AI first lines. How to read a cold-email report without sending one Replacing an unsubscribe link with a coded reply such as “reply banana” is presented as a tactic and carries legal and trust risk wherever permission and opt-out rules apply."
